@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Contact and Entitlement API
	Testing Koroneiki Contact and Entitlement API functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the contact entitlement definitions on koroneiki with the following name values
	| Entitlement Name |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Koroneiki Automotive" for the following products
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Role |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive |

Scenario: Create contact entitlement
	Koroneiki contact entitlements should be able to be created.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                              |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Industry              | Automotive                           |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Notes                 | Additional account notes             |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Sold By               | Liferay US                           |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles	
	| Default Account Role |
	And I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and contact role with the name "Default Account Role" and type "Account" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	Then the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	And the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should be present via the entitlement definition key with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name"

Scenario: Delete contact entitlement definition
	Koroneiki contact entitlement definitions should be able to be deleted.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                              |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Industry              | Automotive                           |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Notes                 | Additional account notes             |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Sold By               | Liferay US                           |
	| Status                | Approved                             |
	| Tier                  | Regular                              |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Role                  |
	| Type        | Account                               |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" to the following roles	
	| Default Account Role |
	And I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}   |                |
	| Perpetual               | true               |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1    | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2    | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3    | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                  |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate} |                |
	And I create a contact entitlement definition related to the product purchase of the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" and contact role with the name "Default Account Role" and type "Account" with the following values
	| Description | Entitlement Description |
	| Name        | Entitlement Name        |
	| Status      | Approved                |
	And I delete a contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name"
	Then the contact entitlement definition with the name "Entitlement Name" should not be present